lized data could be manipulated to run arbitrary code. Instead, consider serializing the relevant data as JSON or a similar text-based serialization format."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.deserialization.pickle.avoid-pickle"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"01b957a8192a3e48d4f891756e26dc862b1281aa8b4916ffc6577eab15f0aaaf4e12d36b36795d271f13072d7d2e7deb1ec043d0defba233e2f18017c95b1957_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"testcode/BenchmarkTest00350.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":58,"snippet":{"text":"\t\t\tproc = subprocess.run(argStr, shell=True, capture_output=True, encoding=\"utf-8\")"},"startColumn":40,"startLine":58}}}],"message":{"text":"Found 'subprocess' function 'run' with 'shell=True'. This is dangerous because this call will spawn the command using a shell process. Doing so propagates current shell settings and variables, which makes it much easier for a malicious actor to execute commands. Use 'shell=False' instead."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"586d6f4f1058b896656c3ebfd88b2ed3fb75e113d21f64481679c1d2d4869c4b5f1d47c7177a01e3f2fa4c7929ed8b2aa12ef3b173c73acf6f32e803b9b720d0_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"testcode/BenchmarkTest00368.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":61,"endLine":51,"snippet":{"text":"\t\t\troot = ET.parse(f'{helpers.utils.RES_DIR}/employees.xml')"},"startColumn":11,"startLine":51}}}],"message":{"text":"The native Python `xml` library is vulnerable to XML External Entity (XXE) attacks.  These attacks can leak confidential data and \"XML bombs\" can cause denial of service. Do not use this library to parse untrusted input. Instead  the Python documentation recommends using `defusedxml`."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.use-defused-xml-parse.use-defused-xml-parse"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBase