ng `pickle`, which is known to lead to code execution vulnerabilities. When unpickling, the serialized data could be manipulated to run arbitrary code. Instead, consider serializing the relevant data as JSON or a similar text-based serialization format."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.deserialization.pickle.avoid-pickle"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"8f4b399ac6cd4b8ca9442000da02e1549c912fcbb3273769e3b0bf9a55e3e44c9a3fc7f0ae7070fa0d0fb3fde682f47a35a83520ebe48729a12518d892190c11_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"testcode/BenchmarkTest00606.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":51,"snippet":{"text":"\t\t\tproc = subprocess.run(argStr, shell=True, capture_output=True, encoding=\"utf-8\")"},"startColumn":40,"startLine":51}}}],"message":{"text":"Found 'subprocess' function 'run' with 'shell=True'. This is dangerous because this call will spawn the command using a shell process. Doing so propagates current shell settings and variables, which makes it much easier for a malicious actor to execute commands. Use 'shell=False' instead."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"0540ffee691ff3463c502ed59ab6b883cd03e7c6f0756d0041b97c579d6fccc246e4ecff30ea2f9d5ed5a85e24a66611bd69b145693e79f121ad99846b1bdddc_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"testcode/BenchmarkTest00607.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":54,"snippet":{"text":"\t\t\tproc = subprocess.run(argStr, shell=True, capture_output=True, encoding=\"utf-8\")"},"startColumn":40,"startLine":54}}}],"message":{"text":"Found 'subprocess' function 'run' with 'shell=True'. This is dangerous because this call will spawn the command using a shell process. Doing so propagates current shell settings and variables, which makes it much easier for a malicious actor to execute commands. Use 'shell=False' instead."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"82f46cb94166259bc9e3c992a0ad0475f916d9ae25bfa404e4793216ddf4fc142b74853d8a0f5a1a93a237d2eba1e07b3354964d25808817dd14956608080ce7_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"testcode/BenchmarkTest00608.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":53,"snippet":{"text":"\t\t\tyobj = yaml.load(bar, Loader=yaml.Loader)"},"startColumn":11,"startLine":53}}}],"message":{"text":"Detected the use of an insecure deserialization library in a Flask route. These libraries are prone to code execution vulnerabilities. Ensure user data does not enter this function. To fix this, try to avoid serializing whole objects. Consider instead using a serializer such as JSON."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.flask.security.insecure-deserialization.insecure-deserialization"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"d0aac185da18464a01ee87a046b12ab0a9e152738f8c94aa689472275b35a111bf100c3cce3ce02a0bc3d1dd38d030d166cac6cb90963883f4f0048f6ce8d2df_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"testcode/BenchmarkTest00608.py","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":53,"snippet":{"text":"\t\t\tyobj = yaml.load(bar, Loader=yaml.Loader)"},"startColumn":11,"startLine":53}}}],"message":{"text":"Detected a possible YAML deserialization vulnerability. `yaml.unsafe_load`, `yaml.Loader`, `yaml.CLoader`, and `yaml.UnsafeLoader` are all known to be unsafe methods of deserializing YAML. An attacker with control over the YAML input could create special YAML input that allows the attacker to run arbitrary Python code. This would allow the attacker to steal files, download and install malware, or otherwise take over the machine. Use `yaml.safe_load` or `yaml.SafeLoader` instead."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"python.lang.security.deserialization.avoid-pyyaml-load.avoid-pyyaml-load"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBa